WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.815
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:06.115 --> 00:00:09.733
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:16.656
Unit twenty-eight: Stop, Remember and Try (-ing or to). Today you will see how the meaning changes with -ing and to.

4
00:00:16.956 --> 00:00:19.469
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.433 --> 00:00:23.736
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:25.619
Stop doing.

7
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:28.941
Stop doing means to end an activity.

8
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:30.969
He stopped smoking.

9
00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:34.062
Your turn. Say: Stop doing.

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.122
Stop doing.

11
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:40.059
Stop to do.

12
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.071
Stop to do means to stop in order to do something.

13
00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:46.126
He stopped to rest.

14
00:00:46.717 --> 00:00:49.392
Your turn. Say: Stop to do.

15
00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:53.246
Stop to do.

16
00:00:53.983 --> 00:00:55.251
Remember doing.

17
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.946
Remember doing means to recall a past action.

18
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:00.899
I remember meeting her.

19
00:01:01.483 --> 00:01:04.182
Your turn. Say: Remember doing.

20
00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.325
Remember doing.

21
00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:10.340
Remember to do.

22
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.884
Remember to do means to not forget a duty.

23
00:01:14.483 --> 00:01:16.088
Remember to lock the door.

24
00:01:16.683 --> 00:01:19.742
Your turn. Say: Remember to do.

25
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:23.903
Remember to do.

26
00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:25.616
Try doing.

27
00:01:26.617 --> 00:01:28.547
Try doing means to experiment.

28
00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.476
Try adding salt.

29
00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:33.678
Your turn. Say: Try doing.

30
00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:37.581
Try doing.

31
00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:39.132
Try to do.

32
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:41.930
Try to do means to make an effort.

33
00:01:42.517 --> 00:01:43.518
Try to win.

34
00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:46.456
Your turn. Say: Try to do.

35
00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.324
Try to do.

36
00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:51.899
Forget.

37
00:01:52.883 --> 00:01:54.709
Forget means to not remember.

38
00:01:55.317 --> 00:01:56.399
Don't forget.

39
00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.473
Your turn. Say: Forget.

40
00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:03.195
Forget.

41
00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:05.172
Meaning change.

42
00:02:06.183 --> 00:02:08.589
Meaning change means a difference in meaning.

43
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:10.637
There is a meaning change.

44
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.763
Your turn. Say: Meaning change.

45
00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:17.903
Meaning change.

46
00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.664
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.517 --> 00:02:27.525
Visal, what is the difference between stop doing and stop to do?

48
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:37.355
He stopped smoking means he quit. He stopped to smoke means he paused another activity in order to smoke. The form changes the meaning.

49
00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:39.857
What about remember?

50
00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:54.147
Remember doing is about a memory: I remember meeting her. Remember to do is about a duty: Remember to lock the door. Forget works the same way: I forgot to call, I'll never forget meeting her.

51
00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.565
And try?

52
00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:09.988
Try doing is an experiment: Try adding more salt. Try to do is an effort that may fail: I tried to open the door, but it was locked. Each verb has two patterns.

53
00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:12.552
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:13.417 --> 00:03:18.052
Grammar focus: Stop and remember and try plus -ing or to-infinitive.

55
00:03:18.352 --> 00:03:19.539
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.983
He stopped smoking (he quit).

57
00:03:22.883 --> 00:03:25.080
He stopped to rest (in order to rest).

58
00:03:25.983 --> 00:03:27.716
Remember to lock the door.

59
00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:41.477
Stop doing = end it. Stop to do = pause in order to. Remember / forget doing = memory. Remember / forget to do = duty. Try doing = experiment. Try to do = effort.

60
00:03:42.217 --> 00:03:46.369
Be careful! Don't say: He stopped to smoke. He quit.

61
00:03:48.333 --> 00:03:51.543
Say: He stopped smoking. He quit.

62
00:03:51.843 --> 00:03:53.436
Stop doing means quit.

63
00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:57.083
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:57.867 --> 00:03:59.425
Same Verb, New Meaning.

65
00:03:59.725 --> 00:04:01.980
My uncle stopped smoking last year.

66
00:04:02.967 --> 00:04:05.082
On the road, he stopped to rest.

67
00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:08.159
I remember meeting you at the festival.

68
00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:11.143
Please remember to lock the door.

69
00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:15.944
Try adding more salt, but I tried to open the door and could not.

70
00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:20.896
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.214
He stopped blank because it was bad for his health.

72
00:04:24.514 --> 00:04:27.668
A, to smoke. B, smoking. C, smoke.

73
00:04:31.233 --> 00:04:33.453
The answer is B: smoking.

74
00:04:34.617 --> 00:04:36.918
Remember blank the door before you leave.

75
00:04:37.218 --> 00:04:40.488
A, locking. B, to lock. C, lock.

76
00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:45.882
The answer is B: to lock.

77
00:04:47.017 --> 00:04:49.411
I tried blank the window, but it was stuck.

78
00:04:49.711 --> 00:04:52.993
A, to open. B, opening. C, open.

79
00:04:56.533 --> 00:04:58.417
The answer is A: to open.

80
00:04:59.583 --> 00:05:01.606
'I remember seeing her' means blank.

81
00:05:01.906 --> 00:05:06.256
A, I recall it. B, I must do it. C, I will do it.

82
00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.753
The answer is A: I recall it.

83
00:05:12.917 --> 00:05:15.694
According to the reading, what did the uncle stop?

84
00:05:15.994 --> 00:05:19.079
A, smoking. B, running. C, working.

85
00:05:22.633 --> 00:05:24.273
The answer is A: smoking.

86
00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:28.549
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:29.383 --> 00:05:33.519
Write two sentences that show the difference between 'stop doing' and 'stop to do'.

88
00:05:42.317 --> 00:05:43.805
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:44.105 --> 00:05:57.918
My father stopped drinking coffee because it kept him awake. On the way home, he stopped to buy some bread. In the first sentence he quit an activity, and in the second he paused in order to do something.

90
00:05:58.218 --> 00:06:00.020
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:00.917 --> 00:06:06.762
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and stop and remember and try plus -ing or to-infinitive.

92
00:06:07.062 --> 00:06:11.850
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

93
00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:15.035
See you in Unit twenty-nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:15.335 --> 00:06:17.848
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

